      "crowdsourced_ai_results": [
        {
          "analysis": "This is a MIPS variant of the Mozi P2P botnet. The malware spreads by exploiting multiple known IoT vulnerabilities, including HNAP and SOAP-based command injections, and a specific Huawei router RCE (CVE-2017-17215). It establishes persistence via `/etc/rc.local` and init scripts. It also modifies `iptables` firewall rules to allow its P2P communication and downloads further payloads. The presence of numerous strings like 'Mozi.m', 'Mozi.a' and DHT-related tags like '[idp]' and '[hp]' confirm its identity as Mozi.",
          "source": "palm",
